<figure class="marketplace-flow" aria-labelledby="marketplace-flow-caption">
  <p class="flow-text-alternative">
    Purchase lines, contextual mappings, and engagement events begin at different levels
    of detail. Engagement is aggregated first; mapping, totals, and unmatched records are
    then checked before the reconciled dataset is used for BI reporting. Exceptions remain
    visible for review.
  </p>
  <ol class="flow-stages">
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Transaction detail</span>
      <strong>Purchase and line-item inputs</strong>
      <small>Start with the records that define the reporting base.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Reference context</span>
      <strong>Posting and customer context</strong>
      <small>Add meaning while retaining missing or uncertain relationships.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Aggregated events</span>
      <strong>Separately aggregated engagement</strong>
      <small>Summarize clicks and applications before joining them to detail.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Controls</span>
      <strong>Grain and relationship controls</strong>
      <small>Check keys, mappings, one-sided activity, and unmatched records.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">Reviewable output</span>
      <strong>Reconciled reporting dataset</strong>
      <small>Keep intended reporting rows and non-additive measures explicit.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="stage-type">BI and review</span>
      <strong>BI reporting and documented exceptions</strong>
      <small>Send reporting output and its exception trail forward together.</small>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="validation-track">
    <strong>Validation travels with the output</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Keys</li>
      <li>Totals</li>
      <li>Exceptions</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="marketplace-flow-caption" class="caption">
    A generic reporting flow showing how sources at different levels of detail can be
    prepared, aggregated, reconciled, and accompanied by visible exceptions before BI
    reporting.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

